{
"cells": [
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"# OLIST E-Commerce Customer Satisfaction Analysis"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 1. Import Required Libraries"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"import pandas as pd\n",
"import numpy as np"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 2. Load Datasets"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"orders = pd.read_csv('olist_orders_dataset.csv')\n",
"customers = pd.read_csv('olist_customers_dataset.csv')\n",
"order_items = pd.read_csv('olist_order_items_dataset.csv')\n",
"payments = pd.read_csv('olist_order_payments_dataset.csv')\n",
"reviews = pd.read_csv('olist_order_reviews_dataset.csv')\n",
"products = pd.read_csv('olist_products_dataset.csv')\n",
"sellers = pd.read_csv('olist_sellers_dataset.csv')"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 3. Customer Dataset Validation"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Total transaction-level customer IDs\n",
"customers['customer_id'].nunique()"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Total actual unique customers\n",
"customers['customer_unique_id'].nunique()"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"### Insight:\n",
"- customer_id represents transaction-level IDs.\n",
"- customer_unique_id represents actual unique customers.\n",
"- One customer can place multiple orders."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 4. Orders Dataset Cleaning"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Convert date columns into datetime format\n",
"\n",
"date_columns = [\n",
"    'order_purchase_timestamp',\n",
"    'order_approved_at',\n",
"    'order_delivered_carrier_date',\n",
"    'order_delivered_customer_date',\n",
"    'order_estimated_delivery_date'\n",
"]\n",
"\n",
"for col in date_columns:\n",
"    orders[col] = pd.to_datetime(orders[col], errors='coerce')"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Standardize order status values\n",
"\n",
"orders['order_status'] = orders['order_status'].str.capitalize()\n",
"\n",
"orders['order_status'] = orders['order_status'].str.replace(\n",
"    'Canceled',\n",
"    'Cancelled'\n",
")"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Check duplicate order IDs\n",
"\n",
"orders['order_id'].duplicated().sum()"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"### Insight:\n",
"- No duplicate order IDs found.\n",
"- Data integrity is maintained."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 5. Temporal Validation Checks"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Check invalid records where delivery happened before approval\n",
"\n",
"invalid_orders = orders[\n",
"    orders['order_approved_at'] >\n",
"    orders['order_delivered_customer_date']\n",
"]\n",
"\n",
"invalid_orders"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Percentage of invalid records\n",
"\n",
"len(invalid_orders) * 100 / len(orders)"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"### Insight:\n",
"- Around 0.06% of records contained logical inconsistencies.\n",
"- These records were removed to maintain data quality."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Remove invalid records\n",
"\n",
"orders = orders[\n",
"    orders['order_delivered_customer_date'] >=\n",
"    orders['order_approved_at']\n",
"]"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Check impossible delivery timelines\n",
"\n",
"invalid_carrier = orders[\n",
"    orders['order_delivered_customer_date'] <\n",
"    orders['order_delivered_carrier_date']\n",
"]\n",
"\n",
"invalid_carrier"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"len(invalid_carrier) * 100 / len(orders)"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"### Insight:\n",
"- Very few records showed impossible delivery flow.\n",
"- These records were removed to preserve analytical accuracy."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Remove invalid carrier records\n",
"\n",
"orders = orders[\n",
"    orders['order_delivered_customer_date'] >=\n",
"    orders['order_delivered_carrier_date']\n",
"]"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 6. Feature Engineering"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Create delivery time feature\n",
"\n",
"orders['delivery_time_days'] = (\n",
"    orders['order_delivered_customer_date'] -\n",
"    orders['order_purchase_timestamp']\n",
").dt.days"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Create delay feature\n",
"\n",
"orders['delay_days'] = (\n",
"    orders['order_delivered_customer_date'] -\n",
"    orders['order_estimated_delivery_date']\n",
").dt.days"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Create earliness feature\n",
"\n",
"orders['earliness_days'] = (\n",
"    orders['order_estimated_delivery_date'] -\n",
"    orders['order_delivered_customer_date']\n",
").dt.days"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Identify same-day deliveries\n",
"\n",
"orders['delivery_type'] = orders['delivery_time_days'].apply(\n",
"    lambda x: 'Same_Day' if x == 0 else 'Standard'\n",
")"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Create late delivery flag\n",
"\n",
"orders['late_delivery'] = (\n",
"    orders['delay_days'] > 0\n",
").astype(int)"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"### Insight:\n",
"- Feature engineering helps transform raw operational data into business insights.\n",
"- late_delivery is useful for customer satisfaction analysis."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 7. Delivery Performance Analysis"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"orders['delivery_time_days'].describe()"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"orders['delay_days'].describe()"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Percentage of delayed deliveries\n",
"\n",
"late_percentage = (\n",
"    len(orders[orders['late_delivery'] == 1]) * 100\n",
"    / len(orders)\n",
")\n",
"\n",
"late_percentage"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"### Insight:\n",
"- Only a small percentage of orders are delayed.\n",
"- However, delays may significantly affect customer experience."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 8. Review Dataset Cleaning"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"reviews.info()"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Check duplicate reviews\n",
"\n",
"reviews['order_id'].duplicated().sum()"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Sort reviews by latest review timestamp\n",
"\n",
"reviews = reviews.sort_values('review_answer_timestamp')"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Keep latest review only\n",
"\n",
"reviews = reviews.drop_duplicates(\n",
"    subset='order_id',\n",
"    keep='last'\n",
")"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Keep required columns\n",
"\n",
"reviews = reviews[['order_id', 'review_score']]"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"### Insight:\n",
"- Some orders had multiple reviews.\n",
"- Keeping the latest review captures final customer sentiment."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 9. Merge Orders and Reviews"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"customer_satisfaction = orders.merge(\n",
"    reviews,\n",
"    on='order_id',\n",
"    how='inner'\n",
")"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 10. Customer Satisfaction Analysis"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Average review score\n",
"\n",
"customer_satisfaction['review_score'].mean()"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Review score distribution\n",
"\n",
"customer_satisfaction.groupby('review_score')['review_score'].count()"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Create review categories\n",
"\n",
"customer_satisfaction['review_category'] = pd.cut(\n",
"    customer_satisfaction['review_score'],\n",
"    bins=[0, 2, 3, 5],\n",
"    labels=['Bad (1-2)', 'Neutral (3)', 'Good (4-5)']\n",
")"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Review category percentage distribution\n",
"\n",
"review_distribution = (\n",
"    customer_satisfaction['review_category']\n",
"    .value_counts(normalize=True) * 100\n",
")\n",
"\n",
"review_distribution"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"### Insight:\n",
"- Most customers provided positive ratings.\n",
"- Negative reviews still provide valuable operational insights."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 11. Impact of Late Delivery on Customer Satisfaction"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Average review score for late vs on-time deliveries\n",
"\n",
"customer_satisfaction.groupby(\n",
"    'late_delivery'\n",
")['review_score'].mean()"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Create bad review flag\n",
"\n",
"customer_satisfaction['is_bad_review'] = (\n",
"    customer_satisfaction['review_score'] <= 2\n",
").astype(int)"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Probability analysis\n",
"\n",
"p_late = customer_satisfaction[\n",
"    customer_satisfaction['late_delivery'] == 1\n",
"]['is_bad_review'].mean()\n",
"\n",
"p_not_late = customer_satisfaction[\n",
"    customer_satisfaction['late_delivery'] == 0\n",
"]['is_bad_review'].mean()\n",
"\n",
"increase = (p_late - p_not_late) * 100\n",
"\n",
"print('P(Bad | Late):', round(p_late * 100, 2), '%')\n",
"print('P(Bad | On-Time):', round(p_not_late * 100, 2), '%')\n",
"print('Increase in probability:', round(increase, 2), '%')"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## Final Business Insight\n",
"\n",
"- Delayed deliveries significantly increase the probability of bad reviews.\n",
"- Delivery performance is one of the major drivers of customer satisfaction.\n",
"- Reducing operational delays can improve customer retention and marketplace reputation."
]
}
],
