      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 6. Data Cleaning – Products Table"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "products.info()\\n",
        "products.isnull().sum()\\n",
        "products.duplicated().sum()\\n",
        "\\n",
        "# Remove rows with missing product information\\n",
        "products = products.dropna()"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Insight\\n",
        "Missing product metadata can affect product-level analysis, therefore incomplete rows were removed."
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 7. Data Cleaning – Order Items Table"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "order_items.info()\\n",
        "order_items.isnull().sum()\\n",
        "\\n",
        "# Keep unique order-seller combinations\\n",
        "order_items = order_items[['order_id', 'seller_id']].drop_duplicates()"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Business Logic\\n",
        "The original dataset contains item-level granularity. Since the analysis focuses on seller performance, duplicate order-seller combinations were removed."
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 8. Feature Engineering"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Create customer fact table\\n",
        "CUSTOMER_FACT = orders.merge(customers, on='customer_id', how='inner')"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Merge seller information into customer satisfaction dataset\\n",
        "CSS = CSS.merge(order_items, on='order_id', how='left')"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Create delay buckets\\n",
        "CSS['Delay_Buckets'] = pd.cut(\\n",
        "    CSS['Delay'],\\n",
        "    bins=[-np.inf, 0, 2, 5, np.inf],\\n",
        "    labels=['On Time / Early', '1-2 Days', '3-5 Days', '5+ Days'],\\n",
        "    right=False\\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Separate late and early deliveries\\n",
        "CSS['late_delay'] = CSS['Delay'].clip(lower=0)\\n",
        "CSS['early_days'] = (-CSS['Delay']).clip(lower=0)"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Insight\\n",
        "Delay buckets help identify operational thresholds where customer dissatisfaction increases sharply."
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 9. Seller Performance Analysis"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "seller_metrics = CSS.groupby('seller_id').agg(\\n",
        "    avg_delay=('Delay', 'mean'),\\n",
        "    median_delay=('Delay', 'median'),\\n",
        "    pct_late=('Delay', lambda x: (x > 0).mean() * 100),\\n",
        "    pct_early=('Delay', lambda x: (x < 0).mean() * 100),\\n",
        "    avg_late_delay=('late_delay', lambda x: x[x > 0].mean()),\\n",
        "    avg_early_days=('early_days', lambda x: x[x > 0].mean()),\\n",
        "    order_count=('order_id', 'count')\\n",
        ").reset_index()"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Create seller volume segments\\n",
        "seller_metrics['volume_segment'] = pd.qcut(\\n",
        "    seller_metrics['order_count'],\\n",
        "    q=3,\\n",
        "    labels=['Low', 'Medium', 'High']\\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Create seller delay segments\\n",
        "seller_metrics['Delay_segments'] = pd.cut(\\n",
        "    seller_metrics['pct_late'],\\n",
        "    bins=[0, 20, 50, 100],\\n",
        "    labels=['Low Delay', 'Moderate Delay', 'High Delay']\\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Key Insight\\n",
        "High-delay sellers show the worst customer satisfaction scores, but most total dissatisfaction originates from high-volume sellers because of their large transaction volume."
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 10. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Average review score by delay bucket\\n",
        "CSS.groupby('Delay_Buckets')['review_score'].mean()"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Percentage of bad reviews by delay bucket\\n",
        "CSS.groupby('Delay_Buckets')['review_category'].value_counts(normalize=True) * 100"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Seller delay impact analysis\\n",
        "seller_metrics.groupby(['volume_segment', 'Delay_segments'])['order_count'].sum()"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### EDA Insight 1\\n",
        "Customer ratings decline significantly when delivery delays exceed 3–5 days."
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### EDA Insight 2\\n",
        "Bad reviews increase sharply for orders delayed more than 5 days, indicating a critical operational threshold."
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### EDA Insight 3\\n",
        "Moderate delays from high-volume sellers contribute more to overall dissatisfaction than extreme delays from low-volume sellers."
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 11. Repeat Purchase Analysis"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Create customer metrics dataset\\n",
        "CUSTOMER_METRICS = CSS.drop_duplicates(subset=['order_id', 'customer_id'])"
      ]
    },

    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Analyze repeat orders\\n",
        "CUSTOMER_FACT.groupby('customer_unique_id')['order_id'].count().sort_values(ascending=False)"
